--- parity notes (web source: features/admin/components/devtools/ToolCard.tsx) ---
* Pure presentational container: GlassPanel(p-5) -> header[ accent icon box(40dp, rounded-lg, bg/.10 + ring/.20),
  title(PanelTitle == h3 text-sm semibold), description(HelperText == p text-xs secondary) ] + content slot (children).
* Accent fromRaw reproduces ICON_COLOR_MAP[color] ?? cyan; dark tokens == web neon hex exactly
  (cyan->status.info #00F0FF, green->status.success #10B981, amber->status.warning #F59E0B,
   red->status.danger #EF4444, purple->chart.power #A855F7).
* No data sources (prompt: "none - pure presentational"); therefore NO loading/error/stale/offline
  lifecycle is invented (would be drift). Genuine container states rendered: content + empty-content
  (null content -> shared EmptyState "No data available", never a blank box) + unknown-accent fallback.
* i18n: source has no literals of its own (title/description are pre-translated props); the empty
  fallback resolves R.string.translation_common_noData (P1/S10). No hardcoded English in shipped code.
* Telemetry: stateful ToolCard emits view.opened {surface: "ToolCard"} via the P1/S11 Logger.
* a11y: icon box is decorative (no contentDescription); title/description are TalkBack-readable text nodes.

